       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, and there is no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nThe order may be a typo or a mix-up with the total daily dose. Here are some options:\n- **1600 mg/day total:** 400 mg by mouth four times daily.\n- **2400 mg/day total:** 800 mg by mouth three times daily.\n- **3200 mg/day (the maximum):** 800 mg by mouth four times daily. This is usually reserved for specific indications, such as inflammatory arthritis, and should be used for the shortest time possible.\n\nTell me the dose you intended, or confirm that 1600 mg four times daily is deliberate and give the clinical reason. I'll enter the order once that's settled. If you do want a dose above the usual maximum, it should also be reviewed by pharmacy or the attending."
      }
