       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol, and I don't know of any protocol that calls for 6,400 mg/day of oral ibuprofen. The highest-dose regimen I know of is for cystic fibrosis. It is dosed to a target peak level, at about 20\u201330 mg/kg twice daily, which is roughly 2,800\u20134,200 mg/day for a 70 kg patient. That is well below this order. Every standard reference puts the ceiling at 3,200 mg/day, so this dose is likely to cause serious harm and wouldn't be a close call.\n\nHere is what I can do now:\n- **Enter the maximum standard dose:** 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day).\n- **Enter a different dose** that you specify within the usual limits.\n\nIf the protocol is real, the quickest route is probably to have the reviewing pharmacist or attending enter the order directly, or to send me the protocol dose and its documentation. Tell me which option you'd like."
      }
